<p style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;"><strong><span>Every Level Exam you take in this course is a "Practice" exam, which means you're practicing for the Certification exam. If you score 80% or higher on all the "Practice" exams in Testing mode, you&rsquo;ll qualify to take the Certification exam for free.</span></strong></span></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<hr />
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><span style="font-size: 18pt;"><strong>Training Mode vs. Testing Mode of the Practice Exam</strong></span></span></p>
<p><strong><img style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;" src="https://github.com/dsquireazva/foundations-of-digital-literacy/blob/main/ExamImages/Test001.png?raw=true" /><br /></strong></p>
<ul>
    <li>
        <p><span style="background-color: #fbeeb8;"><strong>Training Mode:</strong></span></p>
        <ul>
            <li>Contains 45 questions.</li>
            <li>Not timed, so you can take your time.</li>
            <li>You receive immediate feedback on each question as you answer.</li>
            <li>This version helps you learn and practice without pressure.</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p><span style="background-color: #bfedd2;"><strong>Testing Mode:</strong></span></p>
        <ul>
            <li>Also has 45 questions.</li>
            <li>Timed: You have 50 minutes to complete the entire test.</li>
            <li>You need to score at least 700 to pass.</li>
            <li>No feedback is given during the test; you get your results only after finishing.</li>
            <li>This version measures your knowledge under real exam conditions.</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Here's a video that helps explain how to use both:</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><iframe title="YouTube video player" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/PhvQA3ExZ_o?si=Tf9vVT4MJXCWWMW5" width="560" height="315" loading="lazy" allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"></iframe></p>
<hr />
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline; font-size: 18pt;"><strong>Using the Training Mode Exam Results</strong></span></p>
<p>After you have completed the practice test in Training Mode, you will be given 2 detailed lists that explain your results, the "Summary" and the "Details" tabs. :</p>
<p><img style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;" src="https://github.com/dsquireazva/foundations-of-digital-literacy/blob/main/ExamImages/Test002.png?raw=true" /></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 14pt;"><strong>Summary Tab:&nbsp;</strong></span></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 12pt;">You see a summary of your score in each of the domains. You will want to focus your study on the domains where you scored the lowest.</span></p>
<p><img style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;" src="https://github.com/dsquireazva/foundations-of-digital-literacy/blob/main/ExamImages/Test003.png?raw=true" /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span style="font-size: 14pt;"><strong>Details Tab: </strong></span></p>
<p>You will be able to see the specific feedback for each question again. You can use this to help you navigate back to the Domain and Lesson you need to review:&nbsp;</p>
<p><img style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;" src="https://github.com/dsquireazva/foundations-of-digital-literacy/blob/main/ExamImages/Test004.png?raw=true" /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span style="font-size: 14pt;"><strong>*HINT*</strong></span> If you exit the testing page and can't see your results anymore, you can always get back to it by clicking on the 3 dots on the Practice exam and clicking "Score Report"</p>
<p><img style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;" src="https://github.com/dsquireazva/foundations-of-digital-literacy/blob/main/ExamImages/Test005.png?raw=true" /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<hr />
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><span style="font-size: 18pt;"><strong>Take the Level 1 Practice Exam in Training Mode</strong></span></span></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><strong>These Instructions will guide you through getting to the&nbsp;<span style="background-color: #fbeeb8;">"Training"&nbsp;</span>version of the Level 1 exam.</strong></span></p>
<ol>
    <li>Please sign in to&nbsp;<a class="inline_disabled external" style="color: #0035f0;" title="Link" href="https://gmetrix.net/Login.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GMetrix.&nbsp;</a></li>
    <li>Navigate to the IC3 Digital Literacy Level 1 course
        <ul>
            <li><img src="https://github.com/dsquireazva/foundations-of-digital-literacy/blob/main/GMetrixCourseCard%20Level%201.png?raw=true" /></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>Under the courses, you will see the "Digital Literacy Level 1 Practice Exam 1" or "Digital Literacy Level 1 Practice Exam 2". Click "Start"<br />
        <ul>
            <li><img src="https://github.com/dsquireazva/foundations-of-digital-literacy/blob/main/ExamImages/PracticeExam001a.png?raw=true" /></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>Click the Mode dropdown arrow and switch from "Testing" to "Training"
        <ul>
            <li><img src="https://github.com/dsquireazva/foundations-of-digital-literacy/blob/main/ExamImages/PracticeExam001b.png?raw=true" /></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>This will set the test to provide immediate feedback on your answers. When you are ready click "Start Test"
        <ul>
            <li><img src="https://github.com/dsquireazva/foundations-of-digital-literacy/blob/main/ExamImages/PracticeExam002.png?raw=true" /></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>Once you are in the test you will answer a question, then click next. At the top of the page you will see either "Your answer is correct!" or "Your answer is NOT correct!".&nbsp;</li>
</ol>
<ul style="list-style-type: circle;">
    <li><img src="https://github.com/dsquireazva/foundations-of-digital-literacy/blob/main/ExamImages/PracticeExam003.png?raw=true" /></li>
    <li><img src="https://github.com/dsquireazva/foundations-of-digital-literacy/blob/main/ExamImages/PracticeExam004.png?raw=true" /></li>
</ul>
<p>You will then see your answers and if they were incorrect, you will be given the correct answers. You will also see an explanation of the answer in a box at the bottom of the page:&nbsp;</p>
<ul style="list-style-type: circle;">
    <li><img src="https://github.com/dsquireazva/foundations-of-digital-literacy/blob/main/ExamImages/PracticeExam005.png?raw=true" /></li>
</ul>
<p>When you finish, be sure to review the summary and details tabs so you can study more.&nbsp;<span style="font-family: inherit; font-size: 1rem;">Once you have studied more and feel comfortable, you can <span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>move forward to the "Testing" version of the</strong></span></span><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong><span style="font-family: inherit; font-size: 1rem;">&nbsp;</span></strong><strong><span>Lev</span>el 1 Practice Exam assignment</strong></span><span style="font-family: inherit; font-size: 1rem;">. That will be the one that scored in the gradebook.</span></p>
